---
import Studio from "../../layouts/Studio.astro";
import RelatedPosts from "../../components/RelatedPosts.astro";
import { SITE, DEFAULT_OG, fmtDate, iso, POSTS } from "../../lib/blog.mjs";

const slug = "hire-web-developer-india-from-us";
const idx = POSTS.findIndex((p) => p.slug === slug);
const post = POSTS[idx];

const canonical = `${SITE}/blog/${slug}/`;
const ogImage = post.coverImage ? `${SITE}${post.coverImage}` : DEFAULT_OG;
const primaryTag = post.tags[0] || "Notes";
const readMins = post.readMins;
const showUpdated = post.updatedDate && +new Date(post.updatedDate) > +new Date(post.pubDate);
const updatedLabel = showUpdated ? `Updated ${fmtDate(post.updatedDate)}` : null;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      "@id": `${canonical}#post`,
      headline: post.title,
      description: post.description,
      datePublished: iso(post.pubDate),
      dateModified: iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate),
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Divyansh Sood", url: `${SITE}/`, "@id": `${SITE}/#person` },
      publisher: {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": `${SITE}/#studio`,
        name: "Divyansh Sood® Studio",
        logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: `${SITE}/icon.svg` },
      },
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
      mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": canonical },
      image: ogImage,
      articleSection: primaryTag,
      keywords: post.tags.join(", "),
      wordCount: post.wordCount,
      timeRequired: `PT${readMins}M`,
      speakable: {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        cssSelector: [".post-title", ".post-lead"],
      },
      inLanguage: "en",
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${SITE}/blog/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: post.title, item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
---

<Studio
  title={post.seoTitle ?? `${post.title} · Divyansh Sood`}
  description={post.description}
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle={post.title}
  ogImage={ogImage}
  ogImageW={1200}
  ogImageH={750}
  articlePublished={iso(post.pubDate)}
  articleModified={iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate)}
  tags={post.tags}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <main>
    <header class="post-hero">
      <div class="post-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>{primaryTag}</span>
          <span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span>
          {updatedLabel && <span class="post-updated">{updatedLabel}</span>}
          <span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">{post.description}</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>By Divyansh Sood</span><span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span><span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {post.coverImage && (
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img src={post.coverImage} alt={post.title} width="1200" height="750" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    )}

    <article class="wrap narrow post-body">
<p>If you’re a founder in the US, UK or Europe, you’ve heard both versions of the India story.</p>
<p>Version one: incredible engineering value, half the cost, great English, overnight progress while you sleep. Version two: a $2,000 website that arrived broken, three months late, built by someone you never actually spoke to.</p>
<p>Both versions are true. They describe different markets that happen to share a country. This guide is about telling them apart — written by an Indian developer who works with international clients and has no incentive to pretend the second market doesn’t exist.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-two-markets">The two markets</h2>
<p><strong>Market one: the body shops.</strong> Agencies selling hours in bulk. The person who sold you never writes code; the person writing code never talked to you. Your project is a ticket queue. The price looks unbeatable because the unit being sold is time, not outcomes — and rework time bills too.</p>
<p><strong>Market two: senior independents.</strong> A newer generation — developers who could work at product companies but chose independence, who design and code themselves, ship for global clients, and communicate like the remote-native professionals they are. You work with the actual maker, in writing, against outcomes.</p>
<p>The tragedy of “hiring in India” horror stories is that buyers price-shopped their way into market one while believing they were hiring market two.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-fair-pricing-actually-looks-like">What fair pricing actually looks like</h2>
<p>Real numbers, so you can calibrate:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Under ~$1,000 for a full custom site:</strong> market one. Something in the scope is fictional — usually the “custom” part, sometimes the deadline.</li>
<li><strong>~$3,000–10,000:</strong> the honest range for a senior independent building a custom-coded marketing site, storefront or scoped MVP. My own projects start at $3,000 — a US agency quotes the same build at $15,000–40,000.</li>
<li><strong>$10,000+:</strong> product-grade web apps, complex ecommerce, multi-phase builds.</li>
</ul>
<p>You’re not saving 90% by hiring in India. You’re saving the 50–70% that was agency overhead — while the engineering quality, at the senior end, is identical. Chasing the missing 90% is how you end up in market one.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-vetting-checklist">The vetting checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Talk to the person who’ll write the code.</strong> If you can’t, walk. This single filter removes most of market one.</li>
<li><strong>Live production URLs.</strong> Open their work on your phone. Fast? Polished? Still online? Portfolios lie; production doesn’t.</li>
<li><strong>A written scope within 48 hours.</strong> What ships, what it costs, what’s explicitly out. Seniors volunteer this.</li>
<li><strong>Code ownership in writing.</strong> Full repository, IP transfer on final payment. Standard for market two, mysteriously complicated in market one.</li>
<li><strong>Async fluency.</strong> Clear written English, Loom walkthroughs, staging links without being asked. The IST timezone (UTC+5:30) means your morning overlaps their evening — enough for a daily sync, and progress lands while you sleep.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id="how-the-engagement-actually-runs">How the engagement actually runs</h2>
<p>With a senior independent, a typical build looks like: a scoping call, a fixed written quote, milestone payments, a staging URL updated continuously, and handover with documentation. My fastest full build — a <a href="/projects/modernkbs/">site plus admissions portal</a> — took seven days; typical is three to four weeks. That cadence is normal for market two, not exceptional.</p>
<p>One more thing worth demanding from any offshore build: portability. The site should run anywhere — no dependence on the developer’s hosting, no platform you can’t leave. I’ve written up why that matters in <a href="/blog/own-your-stack-code-portability/">own your stack</a>.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>I’m Divyansh Sood, an independent developer in Himachal Pradesh, India, building custom-coded sites, stores and <a href="/services/web-app-development/">web apps</a> for founders in the US, UK and Europe — from $3,000, fixed quotes in writing, full code ownership. If you want to calibrate against a real one before you hire anyone, <a href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com">email me your brief</a> — I’ll respond within a day with an honest scope, even if the honest answer is that you don’t need me.</em></p>
      <div class="tags">{post.tags.map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
    </article>

    <RelatedPosts slug={slug} audience={post.audience} />

    <section class="post-foot-cta">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        {post.audience === "indian-smb" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something in India?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST — I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919816091875" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Message me on WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : post.audience === "d2c-brand" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Building a brand a theme can't carry?</h2>
            <p>If your store has a model that off-the-shelf builders fight — hand-numbered drops, creator commerce, premium D2C — tell me about it. I read every brief personally.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something similar?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. I reply personally, usually within a couple of hours — and I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://calendly.com/sood-divyansh007/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Book a 15-min intro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Studio>
